   "urlId": "sage-payment-services-outage",
   "title": "Sage Payment Services Outage? (Update: It's Back Up and Running)",
   "sourceUrl": "",
   "body": "<div class=\"sqs-layout sqs-grid-12 columns-12\" data-layout-label=\"Post Body\" data-type=\"item\" data-updated-on=\"1673028122825\" id=\"item-62d9abbb9a630f3a59048f48\"><div class=\"row sqs-row\"><div class=\"col sqs-col-12 span-12\"><div class=\"sqs-block html-block sqs-block-html\" data-block-type=\"2\" data-border-radii=\"&#123;&quot;topLeft&quot;:&#123;&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0&#125;,&quot;topRight&quot;:&#123;&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0&#125;,&quot;bottomLeft&quot;:&#123;&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0&#125;,&quot;bottomRight&quot;:&#123;&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0&#125;&#125;\" data-sqsp-block=\"text\" id=\"block-f9519e7e65485b2de74b\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\">\n\n<div class=\"sqs-html-content\" data-sqsp-text-block-content>\n  <p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Apparently Sage Payment Services is suffering an outage. Our 90 Minds Members have reported they haven’t been able to process credit card transactions in the aftermath of Hurricane Sandy. When attempting to process – at least two were presented with the following dialog box. </p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n</div></div><div class=\"sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-code code-block\" data-block-css=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.code/147086af-c803-4086-8ad4-958c4388b836_1125/website.components.code.styles.css&quot;]\" data-block-scripts=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.code/147086af-c803-4086-8ad4-958c4388b836_1125/website.components.code.visitor.js&quot;]\" data-block-type=\"1337\" data-definition-name=\"website.components.code\" data-sqsp-block=\"code\" data-website-component-id=\"bd590816ca4fec051d82\" id=\"block-bd590816ca4fec051d82\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\"><div\n  class=\"sqs-code-container\"\n  \n  \n    data-localized=\"{&quot;enableSafeModeButton&quot;:&quot;Preview in safe mode&quot;,&quot;enableSafeModeText&quot;:&quot;This block contains embedded scripts. Embedded scripts are disabled while you're logged in and editing your site.&quot;,&quot;enableSafeModeTitle&quot;:&quot;Embedded Scripts&quot;,&quot;exitSafeModeButton&quot;:&quot;Exit safe preview&quot;,&quot;exitSafeModeText&quot;:&quot;Please view the page after logging out for accurate rendering.&quot;,&quot;exitSafeModeTitle&quot;:&quot;Safe Preview&quot;,&quot;globalSafeMode&quot;:&quot;Embedded Code: This block contains embedded code that has been disabled.&quot;,&quot;scriptDisabled&quot;:&quot;Script Disabled&quot;}\"\n  \n  \n  \n  \n>\n  \n    <img src=\"http://sp2018tnj6dwj.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/sage-payments-outage.jpg\" title=\"sage-payments-outage\" alt=\"\"/>\n  \n  \n\n\n\n</div>\n\n<style class=\"transform-overrides-vars\">\n  \n</style>\n\n</div></div><div class=\"sqs-block html-block sqs-block-html\" data-block-type=\"2\" data-border-radii=\"&#123;&quot;topLeft&quot;:&#123;&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0&#125;,&quot;topRight&quot;:&#123;&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0&#125;,&quot;bottomLeft&quot;:&#123;&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0&#125;,&quot;bottomRight&quot;:&#123;&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0&#125;&#125;\" data-sqsp-block=\"text\" id=\"block-529d077b0a22398dfe08\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\">\n\n<div class=\"sqs-html-content\" data-sqsp-text-block-content>\n  <p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">The Virtual Terminal has an alert saying they are operating with reduced staff due to Sandy.Apparently SPS is technically closed due to the after effects of Sandy, but a few employees came in to help with the phones, etc. One of the Processing Vendors, based out of NYC, is down. They have been down since 5:15 am, and therefore authorizations and settlements won’t go thru.A mass e-mail was reportedly sent out to all customers at around 10 am ET regarding this outage. No ETA at this point.Update 10:56 am: SPS has updated their portal with information (<a href=\"https://support.sagepayments.com/ics/support/default.asp?deptID=20000\">https://support.sagepayments.com/ics/support/default.asp?deptID=20000</a>).Update 4:00 pm: SPS is back up and running. There was a communication issue with the processor and it has been resolved.via <a href=\"http://www.90minds.com/2012/10/30/sage-payments-down\" target=\"_blank\">90 Minds</a></p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n</div></div></div></div></div>",
